---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="The engineering path and current learning focus of Joshua Brewer."
  ><section class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Systems thinker.<br />Platform builder.</h1><p class="lede">
      Seven-plus years across systems, cloud, and engineering environments have shaped a practical
      approach: understand the system, reduce the friction, and leave it more reliable than you
      found it.
    </p>
  </section><div class="shell stack">
    <section>
      <SectionHeading title="A progression, not a pivot" /><div class="story-grid">
        <p>
          Joshua’s work began in systems, infrastructure, security, and enterprise operations. That
          foundation led to cloud engineering and deep Kubernetes troubleshooting, then into
          platform engineering—where the objective is to build the paved roads that help other
          engineers deliver safely and quickly.
        </p><p>
          His active M.S. in Management Information Systems at Texas A&amp;M University is the next
          expression of that same work: connecting operational data, analytics, and information
          systems to make better engineering decisions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section><section>
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Education" title="Learning in public, with purpose" /><div
        class="credentials"
      >
        <article>
          <h3>M.S. Management Information Systems</h3><p>
            Texas A&amp;M University · Mays Business School
          </p><span>2026 – Present</span>
        </article><article>
          <h3>M.S. Cloud Computing Architecture</h3><p>University of Maryland Global Campus</p><span
            >2021</span
          >
        </article><article>
          <h3>Graduate Certificate, Penetration Testing and Ethical Hacking</h3><p>
            SANS Technology Institute
          </p><span>2024</span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section><section>
      <SectionHeading title="Engineering values" /><div class="pillar-grid">
        <article class="pillar">
          <h3>Make complexity legible</h3><p>
            Good platforms let engineers understand the system and act with confidence.
          </p>
        </article><article class="pillar">
          <h3>Use evidence</h3><p>
            Metrics, logs, events, and clear documentation make better incident decisions.
          </p>
        </article><article class="pillar">
          <h3>Design for the next operator</h3><p>
            Automation and thoughtful defaults turn hard-won knowledge into durable capability.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div></BaseLayout
>
